6. Full Climate Attribution Specification
6.1 Climate Attribution Schema
The climate attribution schema defines the structure of a climate attribution deposit.

It has the following fields:

attribution_id. A string. Required.

attribution_name. A string. Required.

event_or_trend. An object. Required. It contains description, event_type, period, and region.

attributed_cause. An object. Required. It contains cause_name, cause_type, mechanism, and contribution_estimate.

counterfactual_baseline. An object. Required. It contains description and assumptions.

attribution_method. An enum. Required. The values are fraction_of_attributable_risk, probabilistic_event_attribution, trend_attribution, other.

evidence. An array of evidence objects. Required.

models_used. An array of model objects. Optional.

uncertainty. An object. Required. It contains confidence_interval, probability, and sources_of_uncertainty.

confidence_level. An enum. Required. The values are very_high, high, medium, low, very_low.

revisions. An array of revision objects. Optional.

related_attributions. An array of attribution relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

full_pipeline_result_reference. A string. Optional.

null_model_result_reference. A string. Optional.

verification_result_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

The event_or_trend object has:

description. A string.

event_type. An enum. The values are heatwave, drought, flood, storm, wildfire, cold_snap, sea_level_rise, ocean_acidification, glacier_retreat, species_range_shift, crop_yield_change, other.

period. An object. It contains start_date and end_date.

region. An object. It contains region_name, latitude_range, and longitude_range.

The attributed_cause object has:

cause_name. A string.

cause_type. An enum. The values are anthropogenic_greenhouse_gases, anthropogenic_aerosols, land_use_change, volcanic_activity, solar_variation, natural_variability, other.

mechanism. A string.

contribution_estimate. An object. It contains value, units, and confidence_interval.

The counterfactual_baseline object has:

description. A string.

assumptions. An array of strings.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

evidence_type. An enum. The values are observational, model_based, statistical, physical_reasoning, paleoclimate, other.

source_reference. A string.

source_summary. A string.

strength. An enum. The values are strong, moderate, weak, not_assessed.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each model object has:

model_id. A string.

model_name. A string.

model_version. A string.

model_resolution. A string.

ensemble_members. An integer.

model_reference. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

The uncertainty object has:

confidence_interval. An object. It contains lower and upper.

probability. A number. Optional.

sources_of_uncertainty. An array of uncertainty source objects.

Each uncertainty source object has:

source_id. A string.

source_name. A string.

source_description. A string.

source_type. An enum. The values are observational, model_structural, model_parametric, internal_variability, scenario, other.

Each revision object has:

revision_id. A string.

revision_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

revision_description. A string.

previous_position. A string.

new_position. A string.

reason. A string.

source. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each attribution relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_attribution_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_event, same_cause, same_region, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

