7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Climate Attribution
function createClimateAttribution(attribution, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the attribution against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the full-pipeline result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the null-model result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. If the verification result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 7. Generate an attribution ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 8. Insert the climate attribution.

Step 9. Insert the evidence records, the model records, the uncertainty source records, the revision records, and the attribution relations.

Step 10. Insert the links if present.

Step 11. Insert the provenance.

Step 12. Insert the moderation record.

Step 13. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 14. Return the attribution_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Climate Attribution
function readClimateAttribution(attributionId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the attribution. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the evidence, the models, the uncertainty sources, the revisions, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Climate Attribution
function updateClimateAttribution(attributionId, attribution, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing attribution. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new attribution.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the attribution_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Climate Attribution
function deleteClimateAttribution(attributionId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing attribution. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the attribution_id and the status deleted.

